Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when the image stops preinstalling org.gnome.NautilusPreviewer from Flathub.
Subject: core/meta-gnome-core-shell.bst: drop sushi

Sushi is a DBus-activated previewer that Nautilus drives through the
org.gnome.NautilusPreviewer service name. Dakota preinstalls the Flathub
build of the same app instead, so keeping the in-tree element would stage
a second D-Bus service and launcher in the image. The Flatpak is
version-aligned with the pinned GNOME 51 stack.

diff --git a/elements/core/meta-gnome-core-shell.bst b/elements/core/meta-gnome-core-shell.bst
--- a/elements/core/meta-gnome-core-shell.bst
+++ b/elements/core/meta-gnome-core-shell.bst
@@ -23,7 +23,6 @@ depends:
 - core/mutter.bst
 - core/orca.bst
 - core/rygel.bst
-- core/sushi.bst
 - core/tecla.bst
 - sdk/adwaita-icon-theme.bst
 - sdk/glib-networking.bst
